.TH SGRN-SECURITY 5 "July 2026" "SGRN Gateway 1.0" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
security.as \- SGRN Gateway Security Policy Configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/sgrn/security.as
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B security.as
file defines the access control policies for the SGRN Gateway. It uses an embedded AngelScript DSL to configure rules per protocol (S7, HTTP, WebSocket, Modbus, OPC-UA, EtherNet/IP).
.PP
Rules are evaluated in a most-specific-first order. The policy engine is deny-by-default; any request that does not explicitly match an allow rule will be denied.

.SH API REFERENCE
The following factory functions create a \fBPolicyBuilder\fR for a specific protocol:
.TP
\fBs7()\fR
Rules for the native S7 PLC Server.
.TP
\fBhttp()\fR
Rules for the HTTP REST API.
.TP
\fBws()\fR
Rules for the WebSocket Telemetry stream.
.TP
\fBmodbus()\fR
Rules for the Modbus TCP Server.
.TP
\fBopcua()\fR
Rules for the OPC-UA Server.
.TP
\fBeip()\fR
Rules for the EtherNet/IP Adapter.

.SS PolicyBuilder Methods
These methods add conditions to a rule. All conditions must be met for the rule to match.

.TP
\fB.allowIp("x.x.x.x")\fR
Match an exact IPv4 address.
.TP
\fB.allowCidr("x.x.x.x/n")\fR
Match an IPv4 subnet.
.TP
\fB.allowDb(uint16 db_number)\fR
Restrict access to a specific Data Block (S7/Modbus).
.TP
\fB.allowOrigin("http://example.com")\fR
Require a specific Origin header (HTTP/WebSocket).
.TP
\fB.requireHeader("Header-Name")\fR
Require the presence of an HTTP header.
.TP
\fB.allowSession("SessionName")\fR
Require a specific session display name (OPC-UA).
.TP
\fB.allowFieldRead("path")\fR
Restrict read access to a specific field path or subtree. Path can include '*' or '[*]' for array elements.
.TP
\fB.allowField("path")\fR
Restrict both read and write access to a specific field path or subtree.
.TP
\fB.denyFieldWrite("path")\fR
Explicitly deny write access to a specific field path or subtree.

.SS Terminal Actions
Every rule must end with one of the following actions:

.TP
\fB.allow()\fR
Grant access if all conditions are met.
.TP
\fB.deny()\fR
Explicitly deny access if all conditions are met.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Allow HTTP access from a specific subnet, but deny write access to a critical field:
.PP
.nf
    http().allowCidr("192.168.1.0/24")
          .denyFieldWrite("ReactorCore/speed")
          .allow();
.fi

.PP
Allow WebSocket telemetry for a specific origin:
.PP
.nf
    ws().allowOrigin("https://dashboard.local").allow();
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsgrnd\fR(8)
